file: "packages/editor/src/shell/app.tsx"
doc: "The shell finally reads pair.backend, and owns the one asynchronous half of review."

constants: [
  { name: "App"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "App is the entry point and is where the review surface is assembled.\n"
      "It gains the state the two components deliberately do not hold, and\n"
      "the async work the pure functions deliberately cannot do.\n"
      "\n"
      "THREE LOCAL SIGNALS: whether the panel is expanded, which row is\n"
      "selected, and the last sync error. All start closed / undefined.\n"
      "\n"
      "MOUNTING. IslandFrame's slot list is fixed and gains no member. App\n"
      "passes one column into the EXISTING `inspector` slot, holding exactly\n"
      "two children: PendingBanner, and beneath it EITHER PendingPanel when\n"
      "the panel is showing OR Inspector when not. The Inspector is not\n"
      "rendered at all while the panel is open, so expanding replaces it and\n"
      "collapsing brings it back. That slot is the right home because a\n"
      "reviewer is reading rather than editing; a seventh island for a\n"
      "surface that is usually absent would be worse.\n"
      "\n"
      "THE PANEL SHOWS only when `expanded` is true AND the item list is\n"
      "non-empty. Both conditions, not just the signal. Accepting or\n"
      "rejecting the last proposal while expanded would otherwise leave the\n"
      "banner hidden (it renders nothing at zero), the panel empty (it\n"
      "renders nothing with no items) and the Inspector unmounted -- a slot\n"
      "showing nothing, with no control left to bring anything back short of\n"
      "a reload. Tying the panel to the count means the Inspector returns by\n"
      "itself the moment the list empties.\n"
      "\n"
      "THE GEOMETRY GUARD stays on the Inspector alone. That slot is\n"
      "currently wrapped in a Show on scene().geometry(), and the Inspector\n"
      "genuinely cannot render without it -- but the banner and the panel\n"
      "need no geometry, and a layout or render failure is exactly when a\n"
      "reviewer most wants to see what was proposed. So the guard moves\n"
      "inside, around the Inspector branch only.\n"
      "\n"
      "FOCUS. app.tsx keeps a `focusInspector` callback that the Inspector\n"
      "registers on mount and nothing has ever cleared, because until now the\n"
      "Inspector never unmounted. It does now. App sets that callback back to\n"
      "undefined whenever it renders the panel in the Inspector's place,\n"
      "otherwise the focus-inspector command -- Cmd/Ctrl+I, the context menu\n"
      "row and the palette row -- calls a closure over a detached node and\n"
      "silently does nothing. command_wiring.test.ts asserts against spies\n"
      "and would stay green through exactly that failure.\n"
      "\n"
      "Both new components get pendingItems(state().stylesheet()) -- the\n"
      "banner needs only its length, and that same length is what gates the\n"
      "panel above.\n"
      "\n"
      "ACCEPT and REJECT call state().acceptPending / rejectPending and\n"
      "nothing else. Neither contacts a forge: the proposal's fate is local,\n"
      "and pushing it back to a PR is a separate feature nobody asked for.\n"
      "\n"
      "REPLY. Await newComment(body, 'user:local'), call state().addComment\n"
      "FIRST so the comment is stored and undoable even with no network, and\n"
      "only then, when pair.backend is defined, call backend.postComment. A\n"
      "post that resolves Err leaves the comment in place and sets the\n"
      "sync-error signal.\n"
      "\n"
      "FETCH RUNS BEFORE THE EditorState IS CREATED, and that ordering is\n"
      "load-bearing rather than incidental. In loadFrom, once the stylesheet\n"
      "is loaded and before createEditorState, if pair.backend is defined:\n"
      "await fetchThreads(), and on Ok fold the entries in with mergeThreads,\n"
      "then hand the MERGED stylesheet to createEditorState.\n"
      "\n"
      "The alternative -- create the state, then fetch and adoptStylesheet --\n"
      "loses fetched comments. adoptStylesheet writes no undo entry, so the\n"
      "next undo of any edit restores a pendingEditsBefore snapshot taken\n"
      "before the merge and the discussion disappears. Merging first means\n"
      "the comments are part of the document the session starts from, there\n"
      "is nothing to undo past, and addComment is genuinely the only writer\n"
      "of a comment into a live stylesheet.\n"
      "\n"
      "It costs one await before the canvas appears, on sessions that already\n"
      "fetched the diagram over the network. An Err result sets the\n"
      "sync-error signal and starts the session on the unmerged stylesheet,\n"
      "rather than failing the load.\n"
      "\n"
      "SYNC ERROR is cleared at the START of each attempt -- both the fetch\n"
      "above and every postComment -- so a success after a failure removes\n"
      "the message rather than leaving a stale one. Both paths report through\n"
      "the Result the CommentBackend methods return; neither treats a thrown\n"
      "exception as the failure channel.\n"
      "\n"
      "ONE KNOWN COST, accepted rather than solved here: a reply marks the\n"
      "document dirty, so the save controller autosaves it, and because the\n"
      "stylesheet identity changes GhostRender's memo re-runs the full layout\n"
      "and render pipeline. That is the existing ghost cost, now reachable by\n"
      "typing a comment."
    type: { named: { symbol: "Component" } }
    uses: ["PendingBanner", "PendingPanel", "pendingItems", "mergeThreads", "newComment"]
  }
]
